# strict-source-grounding-no-inference

All factual content must be derived exclusively from the provided authoritative source material (the DryWave 3000 manual or equivalent supplied reference). General domain knowledge must not substitute for, augment, or fill gaps in source material. When source material does not address a query, that gap must be surfaced explicitly rather than bridged by inference or general knowledge.

## Procedures
- For every factual claim, verify it is present in the provided source material before including it.
- If a query cannot be answered from source material, state explicitly that the information is not available in the reference document.
- Do not use general dehumidifier or electrical knowledge to fill gaps in the manual.

